### KEY: AP has 0 coincident pairs but DOES have antipodal pairs.
### The 'rotational regular R_13' is the SAME iso class regardless of
### tie-break ONLY IF the antipodal orientation is itself rotationally
### symmetric. Check: does AP's score stay (6,...,6) for ALL a, both
### tie-breaks?  If yes, all a give REGULAR tournaments (score-invariant)
### even if not all literally isomorphic.
  AP under INDEX: (a, regular?, common-score, c3, H):
     (1, True, 6, 91, 3711175)
     (3, False, None, 89, 3394355)
     (5, False, None, 89, 3351471)
